              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2024-41131](https://osv.dev/CVE-2024-41131)**.\n\n## [GHSA-63p8-c4ww-9cg7](https://osv.dev/GHSA-63p8-c4ww-9cg7)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e An Out-of-bounds Write vulnerability has been found in the ImageSharp gif decoder, allowing attackers to cause a crash using a specially crafted gif. This can potentially lead to denial of service.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Patches\n\u003e The problem has been patched. All users are advised to upgrade to v3.1.5 or v2.1.9.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Workarounds\n\u003e None.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### References\n\u003e https://github.com/SixLabors/ImageSharp/pull/2754\n\u003e https://github.com/SixLabors/ImageSharp/pull/2756\n\u003e \n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/sentinelai-fixtures/sentinelai-fixtures/src/OrderApp/packages.lock.json | SixLabors.ImageSharp | 1.0.4 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-63p8-c4ww-9cg7 | SixLabors.ImageSharp | 2.1.9, 3.1.5 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/sentinelai-fixtures/sentinelai-fixtures/src/OrderApp/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2024-41131\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n",
                "text": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2024-41131](https://osv.dev/CVE-2024-41131)**.\n\n## [GHSA-63p8-c4ww-9cg7](https://osv.dev/GHSA-63p8-c4ww-9cg7)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e An Out-of-bounds Write vulnerability has been found in the ImageSharp gif decoder, allowing attackers to cause a crash using a specially crafted gif. This can potentially lead to denial of service.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Patches\n\u003e The problem has been patched. All users are advised to upgrade to v3.1.5 or v2.1.9.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Workarounds\n\u003e None.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### References\n\u003e https://github.com/SixLabors/ImageSharp/pull/2754\n\u003e https://github.com/SixLabors/ImageSharp/pull/2756\n\u003e \n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/home/runner/work/sentinelai-fixtures/sentinelai-fixtures/src/OrderApp/packages.lock.json | SixLabors.ImageSharp | 1.0.4 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-63p8-c4ww-9cg7 | SixLabors.ImageSharp | 2.1.9, 3.1.5 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/home/runner/work/sentinelai-fixtures/sentinelai-fixtures/src/OrderApp/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2024-41131\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n"
